35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"We have a serious staffing shortage in the late-turn pool and general crews, though maintenance for lifts and escalators is surprisingly well-covered.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The mid-city runs are slower than they used to be, but the bottlenecks aren't where people think; it's the connections, not the ticketing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have a ring-fenced construction balance, but operating subsidies are shrinking. Also, ticketing fees are eating into our paving budget.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"Interestingly, a late-evening pilot was successful years ago, but some previous lane-priority projects were quickly reverted to mixed traffic.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Working in pre-war shells is now a high-risk gamble due to unrecorded voids, and the ferry and rail offices are not aligned on data.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if operating subsidies are trimmed, a plan requiring more drivers is a non-starter.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, if the mid-city is slow, maybe a dedicated corridor is the answer, provided the ""voids"" aren't an issue there.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, you're right. We should lean toward capital-funded projects rather than those increasing permanent operating costs.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, remember that lane-priority has failed us before. We should be cautious about dedicated bus lanes.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, the ""voids"" are in the stations, not the streets, but the administrative friction for multi-modal systems is very real.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,Then we should avoid the night extension if the late-turn pool is already exhausted.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"If ticketing isn't the delay, then a new fare platform might be a waste of time.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. Let's focus on where the ring-fenced construction money can be used effectively.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"The success of the evening pilot suggests demand exists, but the staffing issue Asuka mentioned is a critical barrier.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,Station upgrades seem risky given the contingency pricing for those old shells.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
