60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Looking at the candidates, the Station Access Upgrades align with the available maintenance capacity I found.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"The Crosstown Bus Corridor addresses the mid-city slowness, but I'm worried about the lane-priority failures Servas mentioned.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Integrated Fare Platform is too expensive in terms of contractor fees, and the Night Service Extension hits the operating budget.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The Night Service Extension has historical precedent for success, but the current staffing crisis makes it impractical.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Fare Platform has too many committee disagreements. The Bus Corridor is safer than the Station Upgrades regarding ""voids.""","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the Station Access Upgrades use the lift/escalator contract which has spare capacity. It's the most viable operationally.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, if the Bus Corridor is just ""limited-stop"" and not purely ""dedicated lanes,"" does that mitigate the previous failures?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the Station Access Upgrades can be funded by the ring-fenced construction balance. It's the most fiscally sound.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, perhaps, but the Station Access plan is a more stable bet if the maintenance crews are ready.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I still worry about the pre-war shells, but the Bus Corridor's administrative path is clearer than the Fare Platform.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Station Access Upgrades. It's the only one that doesn't break our remaining staff.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'll go with the Bus Corridor. We need to fix the mid-city travel times now.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I support the Station Access Upgrades. It fits the capital ledger perfectly.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,I will vote for Station Access Upgrades. It's a proven need and we have the maintenance capacity.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I'll vote for the Bus Corridor to avoid the risks of the pre-war station shells.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
